---
import SiteLayout from '@nyameko/ui/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="How to Cite" siteName="Quantum Platform" section="User Portal"
  description="Guidance for acknowledging Quantum Platform software and computational resources in research.">
  <section class="section container citation-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">SCIENTIFIC REPRODUCIBILITY</p>
    <h1>How to cite and acknowledge Quantum Platform</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Please make it clear which facility, software, datasets, workflows and
      providers supported your work. Include versioned artefacts and resource
      identifiers where available.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Document what you used</h2>
      <p>In the Methods or Computational Resources section, record the platform components, software versions, experiment or workflow identifiers, dates, CPU/GPU/QPU backends and relevant programme or allocation numbers.</p>
      <p>Link directly to the specific version of the software or scientific workflow where its repository and commit are publicly available.</p>
      <a href="https://github.com/nyameko/quantum-platform">Quantum Platform source</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
      <a href="https://github.com/nyameko/quantum-workflows">Quantum Workflows source</a>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Citation and acknowledgement</h2>
      <p>The official facility citation, acknowledgement template, funding credits and machine-readable citation metadata are being prepared. Please do not invent a DOI, funding number or citation version.</p>
      <p>Until an official citation is published, accurately acknowledge the actual systems and software used and cite any relevant public repository release or reference paper.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Scientific collaboration and authorship</h2>
      <p>
        Collaborations and substantive scientific contributions may merit co-authorship
        by mutual agreement and according to the venue's authorship criteria.
        Merely accessing a shared facility, providing routine support or receiving
        resources does not automatically require authorship for any specific person.
        Recognize other contributions in the acknowledgements.
      </p>
      <p>For guidance, see the
        <a href="https://www.icmje.org/recommendations/browse/roles-and-responsibilities/defining-the-role-of-authors-and-contributors.html">ICMJE authorship and contributor criteria</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p><a href="/publications/">Return to publications</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .citation-page { max-width: 65rem; padding-top: 3rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.8rem); letter-spacing: -.04em; margin: .4rem 0; }
  .citation-page section { margin-top: 1.7rem; }
  .citation-page section:not(:last-child) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .citation-page a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
